9NcLz4Cd8y2SjxpXbEvQE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The nightly failure is fixed and the pull request is open with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Fix:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on the new branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding` (commit `08d3cd5986`). The test expectations match banker's rounding: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **Pull request:** #101, against `main`. It was created by a call that timed out, so the reviewer request didn't go through at first. I confirmed #101 existed and added alex to it with `request_review`, rather than opening a duplicate.\n\nNothing was merged. Merging into `main` needs approval from a code owner.", "type": "text"}]}]}